---
layout: base.njk
title: Contact | The Web3 Family
description: Reach Christopher Clarke directly, or book a free strategy call.
---
{% from "cta.njk" import button %}
<!-- CONTACT -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="subhead">Call, text, email, or book a free strategy call. Whatever is easiest.</p>

    <!--
      This is a stand-in for real ZipForm embed, per direct request
      ("This needs to be a form"). Not the real ZipForm widget: that
      still needs the actual embed snippet or hosted form URL from
      Christopher's own ZipForm account, which nobody but him can
      pull, and loading it will be a deliberate, confirmed exception
      to the site's zero-client-JS rule (section 9), the same kind of
      tradeoff Microsoft Clarity already is. In the meantime this is a
      plain mailto: form: it needs no backend and adds no JavaScript,
      but it only works if the visitor's device has an email app
      configured to handle mailto: links, which not everyone does
      (many people read mail only in a browser tab). Swap this whole
      block for the real ZipForm embed once that's in hand.
    -->
    <form class="contact-form" action="mailto:christopher@theweb3family.com" method="post" enctype="text/plain">
      <label>Name
        <input type="text" name="Name" required>
      </label>
      <label>Email
        <input type="email" name="Email" required>
      </label>
      <label>Message
        <textarea name="Message" rows="5" required></textarea>
      </label>
      <button type="submit" class="cta"><span>Send</span></button>
    </form>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Or reach me directly:</p>
      <p><a href="tel:+13107036003">(310) 703-6003</a>, call or text</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0"><a href="mailto:christopher@theweb3family.com">christopher@theweb3family.com</a></p>
    </div>

    {{ button() }}
  </div>
</section>
